[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Good News]
[00:00.86]What was the good news? | 好消息是什么？
[00:12.88]The secretary told me that Mr. Harmsworth would see me. | 秘书告诉我哈姆斯沃思先生会见我。
[00:18.88]I felt very nervous when I went into his office. | 当我走进他的办公室时，我感到非常紧张。
[00:24.02]He did not look up from his desk when I entered. | 我进去时，他没有从办公桌上抬起头。
[00:28.32]After I had sat down, | 我坐下后，
[00:31.14]he said that business was very bad. | 他说生意很糟。
[00:34.73]He told me that the firm could not afford to pay such large salaries. | 他告诉我公司负担不起支付如此高的薪水。
[00:40.80]Twenty people had already left. | 已经有二十人离开了。
[00:44.68]I knew that my turn had come. | 我知道轮到我了。
[00:48.15]'Mr. Harmsworth,' I said in a weak voice. | “哈姆斯沃思先生，”我用微弱的声音说。
[00:53.12]'Don't interrupt,' he said. | “不要打断，”他说。
[00:55.84]Then he smiled and told me I would receive an extra thousand pounds a year! | 然后他笑了，告诉我每年将额外获得一千英镑！